<?php

namespace App\Libraries;

/**
 * Fourth batch: real situations and requests users and admins meet (InterLink fill flow and PIC responsibility, data
 * lookups, test procedures, bonding, workflow questions, account and privacy, performance, admin tasks).
 * Loaded by `php spark brain:seed`.
 */
class BrainSeed4
{
    /** @return list<array<string,mixed>> */
    public static function all(): array
    {
        $o = static fn (string $label, string $url, bool $admin = false): array => ['type' => 'open', 'label' => $label, 'url' => $url] + ($admin ? ['role' => 'admin'] : []);
        $k = static fn (string $title, string $keywords, string $body, array $steps = [], array $extra = []): array => array_merge(['title' => $title, 'keywords' => $keywords, 'body' => $body, 'steps' => $steps], $extra);
        $dtr = ['page_match' => 'dtr'];
        $il  = ['page_match' => 'interlink'];
        $adm = ['role_min' => 'admin'];

        return [
            // =========================================================== InterLink: filling and sending the report
            $k('I synced to InterLink but nothing changed in InterLink', 'synced but nothing changed, interlink not updated, sync did not update interlink, no report in interlink, report not shown interlink, nothing in interlink after sync', 'Syncing in NEXUS-L prepares the values and records the sync; it does not submit anything inside InterLink. The report is sent only when the person responsible (the PIC) fills the InterLink form in their own browser and presses Save / Submit there. Use "Confirm, Fill & 1-Click Send Report", then follow the steps shown.', ['In the pre-sync dialog press Confirm, Fill & 1-Click Send Report.', 'Press Copy fill data, then Open the InterLink form.', 'On the form click the NEXUS-L fill bookmark.', 'Check the green fields and press Save / Submit yourself.'], $il),
            $k('Who sends the report to InterLink?', 'who submits interlink, who sends report, pic submit, person in charge interlink, responsible for sending, who is responsible interlink, pic', 'The person in charge (PIC) responsible for the report sends it, from their own browser and their own InterLink sign-in. NEXUS-L never submits for them; it only prepares and fills the values so the PIC can review and submit.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I fill the InterLink form with the NEXUS-L values?', 'fill interlink form, autofill interlink, fill form from nexus-l, copy fill data, fill bookmark, nexus-l fill bookmark, fill values interlink', 'In the pre-sync dialog confirm and press "Confirm, Fill & 1-Click Send Report". A panel appears: press "Copy fill data", then "Open the InterLink form", and click the "NEXUS-L fill" bookmark on that form. The matching boxes turn green. Review everything and press Save / Submit yourself.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I install the NEXUS-L fill bookmark?', 'install bookmark, add bookmark, bookmarklet, nexus-l fill bookmark, drag bookmark, bookmarks bar, create bookmark', 'In the fill panel drag the "NEXUS-L fill" button to your bookmarks bar (Ctrl + Shift + B shows the bar). If dragging does not work, press "Copy bookmark code", create a new bookmark named "NEXUS-L fill" and paste the code as its address.', [], $il),
            $k('The NEXUS-L fill bookmark does nothing', 'bookmark does nothing, fill bookmark not working, bookmarklet nothing, fill not working, click bookmark nothing', 'Click the bookmark while the InterLink form is open (not on the NEXUS-L page) and press "Copy fill data" in NEXUS-L first. If nothing happens, the bookmark code may be incomplete: delete it and add it again with "Copy bookmark code".', [], $il),
            $k('The browser asks permission to read the clipboard', 'clipboard permission, allow clipboard, paste permission, clipboard blocked, read clipboard, clipboard prompt', 'The fill bookmark reads the fill data you copied. Allow clipboard access for InterLink when the browser asks; if you decline, it asks you to paste the data into a box instead.', [], $il),
            $k('The fill said some fields were not found', 'fields not found, not found on this page, some fields missing fill, fill partial, interlink fill missing fields, could not fill', 'Those boxes are on another tab or page of the InterLink form. Open the tab that has them (for example the Upload Result tab) and click the bookmark again; fields already filled stay as they are.', [], $il),
            $k('What does the green outline in InterLink mean?', 'green outline, green box, green fields, filled fields green, highlighted green interlink', 'A green outline marks a box that NEXUS-L filled. Check each one against the report before submitting; boxes without an outline were not touched.', [], $il),
            $k('Can NEXUS-L attach the PDF to InterLink?', 'attach pdf interlink, upload pdf interlink, attachment interlink, test report file upload, pdf upload interlink', 'No. Browsers do not allow a page to choose a file for you, so attach the report PDF in InterLink yourself (download it from the report preview first). The file name is prepared as LabRef_TestReport.pdf.', [], $il),
            $k('Do I need to sign in to InterLink to use the fill bookmark?', 'sign in before fill, login interlink to fill, interlink login for bookmark, own session interlink, need login fill', 'Yes, with your own account in your own browser: that is what makes you the sender. The Sync Center connection is separate and only reads the InterLink list for NEXUS-L.', [], $il),
            $k('Is the report in InterLink after I press Fill?', 'is it sent after fill, fill means sent, did fill submit, filled equals submitted, report sent after fill', 'No. Filling only types the values into the form. The report is sent when you press Save / Submit in InterLink.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I check a report really arrived in InterLink?', 'check report arrived, verify in interlink, was report submitted, confirm submission, did interlink receive, check status interlink', 'Open the application in InterLink (or the InterLink list in NEXUS-L after a minute) and check its status and the uploaded report. NEXUS-L\'s Sync History only shows what was prepared, not what InterLink received.', [], $il),
            $k('Why does Sync History say synced but InterLink is empty?', 'sync history synced empty interlink, history says synced, synced flag, synced count, counted as synced', 'Sync History counts the preparations done in NEXUS-L. Only a submission by the PIC in InterLink puts the report there. Fill and submit it again if the InterLink record is empty.', [], $il),
            $k('I filled the wrong application in InterLink', 'wrong application filled, wrong application no, filled wrong interlink, mistake application, wrong report interlink', 'Do not submit. Close the InterLink form without saving, open the correct application and fill again. If it was already submitted, tell the InterLink administrator or your supervisor right away.', [], $il),
            $k('Can several Lab References go into one InterLink application?', 'many lab refs one application, multiple reports one application, several samples application, one app many lab refs', 'Each InterLink application takes the reports it was created for. Use the Application No. that belongs to the request and fill the form for each Lab Reference one at a time; ask your supervisor if you are unsure which application to use.', [], $il),

            // =========================================================== data lookups
            $k('The Material Code is not found', 'material code not found, lookup material fails, unknown material code, no match material code, material lookup empty', 'Check the code for typos and spaces, then press Tab again. If the code is new it may not be in the master list yet: type the description by hand and tell an administrator so it can be added.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The PO / Lot lookup finds nothing', 'po lookup nothing, production code not found, po lot not found, lot lookup fails, prodcode not found', 'Type the production code exactly as on the sample and press Tab. If it is not in the shoe list, fill the style, colour and PO by hand and tell an administrator.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The MTL number is not found in DSR', 'mtl not found, dsr not found, mtl lookup nothing, dsr empty, no dsr record', 'Check the MTL number. If it is not in the DSR list, the DSR boxes stay empty: fill what you know and tell an administrator that the DSR record is missing.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Auto-Lookup filled the wrong material', 'wrong material autofill, lookup wrong material, auto lookup wrong, wrong description filled, lookup mismatch', 'Check the Material Code you typed; the lookup follows it exactly. Correct the code and press Tab, or overwrite the description by hand before saving.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The supplier or style fields are empty after lookup', 'supplier empty, style empty after lookup, lookup did not fill supplier, blank supplier, blank style', 'Those values come from the master lists. If they are missing there, type them by hand; an administrator can add the missing master record so it fills next time.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How often is the master data updated?', 'master data updated, lookup data refreshed, material list updated, new materials added, data refresh master', 'The master lists (materials, shoes, DSR, standards) are maintained by administrators. New items appear after they are added; tell an administrator about anything missing.', [], $dtr),

            // =========================================================== test procedures and readings
            $k('How many thickness readings do I enter?', 'thickness readings, how many thickness, 6 point thickness, thickness 1 to 6, thickness points, thickness specimens', 'Enter Thickness 1 to 6. Min, Max and Average (TAve) are calculated automatically and the thickness-based standards are applied when you press "Refresh & Apply Smart Standards".', [], $dtr),
            $k('How many specimens for weight and specific gravity?', 'weight specimens, how many weight, sg specimens, three specimens, number of samples weight', 'Weight and specific gravity use 3 specimens each; the averages are calculated for you.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How is hardness entered?', 'hardness, shore a, durometer, hardness reading, hardness rating, enter hardness', 'Enter the Shore A hardness readings in the hardness boxes; the average and rating are calculated against the standard for the material.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Where do I enter tensile and elongation results?', 'tensile elongation entry, enter tensile, elongation boxes, tensile l w, warp weft tensile', 'In the physical and mechanical section of the material form. Fabrics have length (L) and width (W) readings; the machine file normally fills them, and the averages and pass/fail follow.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What do L and W mean in the readings?', 'l and w, length width, direction l w, warp weft, tensile l, tensile w, specimen direction', 'L is the length direction and W the width direction of the material. Each direction has its own readings and rating.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How are specimen averages and pass fail worked out?', 'specimen average, ave rule, pass fail rule, average vs standard, pass if average, directional average', 'The average of the specimens in a direction is compared with the standard: average at or above the standard is PASS, otherwise FAIL (some tests have a tolerable band). The worst test decides the overall stamp.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I record a colorfastness result?', 'record colorfastness, enter crocking, crocking dry wet, uv rating, heat aging entry, six fiber grades', 'In the colorfastness section enter the grade for each of the 6 fibres and for crocking (dry and wet), UV and heat aging. Any fibre below the standard makes the result FAIL.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is the Overall Rating (Remarks)?', 'overall rating, remarks field, overall remarks, final rating, overall result remarks, final result', 'The overall rating is the worst result of all tests in the report and sets the PASS / TOLERABLE / FAIL stamp. It is calculated when the Status is Complete.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Can I leave a test blank if it was not done?', 'leave test blank, skip test, not tested, test not required, empty test section, not applicable', 'Yes. Leave the readings of tests that were not required empty; they are not counted in the overall rating.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What if a specimen failed and I retested only that one?', 'retest one specimen, single specimen retest, repeat one specimen, replace specimen, specimen redo', 'Replace that specimen\'s reading with the new value, refresh the standards and save, following your lab procedure for retests. If the procedure requires a separate retest report, create it as a new record with its own Lab Ref No.', [], $dtr),

            // =========================================================== bonding extras
            $k('How do I read the bonding report quickly?', 'read bonding report, understand bonding report, bonding report explained, how to read report, report sections', 'The top shows the sample and result stamp, the table gives Min, Max, the standard and PASS / TOLERABLE / FAIL for each shoe part, and the diagram shows every spot value at its position. The center column lists the filler (FiTO) values.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What are the colours of the values on the shoe diagram?', 'diagram colours, value colours, red amber blue values, colour meaning diagram, blue values red values', 'Values at or above the standard are blue, values in the tolerance band are amber, and values below tolerance are red, so weak spots stand out.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Why is a value missing on the diagram?', 'value missing diagram, spot not shown, missing number shoe, empty spot diagram, no value on point', 'A spot with no reading (a dash in the machine file) is not printed. A hidden point is also not shown: an administrator can show it again in the Report Designer.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I compare left and right shoes?', 'compare left right, compare shoes, left vs right, both sides compare, two shoes results', 'Open the -L and -R reports one after the other from the Lab Tracker; each has its own table and diagram.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I add Mode of Failure or comments to a bonding report?', 'add comments bonding, mode of failure entry, remarks bonding, comment field, write note report', 'Fill "Mode of Failure" in the bonding form (and the comments box if shown) and save. They are printed on the report.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The standard on the bonding table is 2.5 but I expect 3', 'standard 2.5 expect 3, wrong std bonding, std mismatch, adult 3 shows 2.5', 'The standard follows the Age Category: Children is 2.5 and Adult 3.0. Change the Age Category to Adult, recalculate and save. Style names without UA, WM or MN are treated as Adult unless they contain UY, TD, JN or INFANT.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I see the standard used for each shoe part?', 'standard per shoe part, which std used, std per part, upper foxing standard, foxing outsole standard, center standard', 'The table at the top of the bonding report lists the standard for Upper/Foxing Tape, Foxing Tape/OS and Center IS/OS next to the Min and Max values.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I load bonding results for many shoes in a row?', 'many bonding reports, bulk bonding, load many shoes, several u60 files, batch bonding load', 'Load them one at a time: pick or create each report, type its Lab Ref No., press Load U60 Machine File and Save. There is no batch loader yet.', [], $dtr),

            // =========================================================== PIC / workflow / roles
            $k('What is a PIC?', 'what is pic, person in charge, pic meaning, who is pic, pic responsibility', 'PIC means person in charge: the person responsible for a report and for sending it. In NEXUS-L the PIC reviews the values and submits the report in InterLink personally.', [], $il),
            $k('What is the normal workflow from sample to InterLink?', 'workflow, process flow, sample to report, end to end, steps from test to interlink, lab workflow', 'Receive the sample, test it, create or open the report in NEXUS-L, load the machine results, check ratings and save, print or download the PDF, then the PIC syncs the Lab Reference, fills the InterLink form with the NEXUS-L bookmark, attaches the PDF and submits.', ['Create / open the report and load the machine results.', 'Check the ratings and Save.', 'Download the PDF.', 'Sync: pick the Lab Reference and fill the InterLink form.', 'Attach the PDF and submit in InterLink.'], $dtr),
            $k('Who can edit and who can only view?', 'roles permissions, who can edit, who can view, user vs admin, access levels, what can users do', 'Every signed-in user can create and edit reports. Administrators additionally see the Report Designer and the Brain console. If you cannot do something you expect, ask an administrator.'),
            $k('Who approves a report before it is sent?', 'who approves report, approval before sending, reviewer approval, sign off report, approval process', 'Follow your lab\'s approval procedure. In NEXUS-L, "Reviewed By" (bonding) and "Stamp Reviewed" record the review; the PIC then submits in InterLink.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Can I send a report that failed?', 'send failed report, submit fail report, report with fail to interlink, fail result interlink, tolerable report send', 'The result is part of the report and is filled as FAIL, TOLERABLE (Data) or PASS. Whether a failed report is sent immediately or retested first follows your lab procedure; the PIC decides.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I hand a report over to a colleague?', 'hand over report, assign colleague, pass report, transfer report, give report to another', 'Save the report, then tell the colleague the Lab Reference No. (or send it in the Inbox). They find it in the Lab Tracker.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Can I work on reports offline?', 'offline work, no internet work, without network, work offline, cached offline', 'No. NEXUS-L needs a connection to the lab network because reports are saved on the server.'),

            // =========================================================== printing and pdf extras
            $k('How do I include the report attachment page in the bonding PDF?', 'attachment page bonding, include attachment, report attachment, extra page bonding, print attachment', 'The bonding preview and PDF include the shoe diagram sheet. If your report needs an extra attachment page, ask an administrator to add it with the Report Designer.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The PDF shows the wrong logo or no SATRA mark', 'wrong logo pdf, satra missing pdf, logo pdf wrong, no accreditation mark, logos not in pdf', 'Download PDF always includes the VF logo (left) and the SATRA mark (right). Reload with Ctrl + F5 and download again; if a logo is still wrong tell an administrator.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I print only the diagram?', 'print only diagram, print shoe only, only the sketch, print diagram page', 'There is no diagram-only print. Print the whole sheet or crop the page from the PDF.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I print in colour or black and white?', 'colour print, black and white print, print colour, grayscale, mono print', 'Choose Color or Black and white in your printer dialog. The pass / tolerable / fail colours are also marked by text, so a black and white copy is still readable.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Can I print the report without the logos?', 'print without logo, remove logos print, no logo print, logos off', 'No; the logos are part of the official sheet. An administrator can change the layout if a version without them is needed.', [], $dtr),

            // =========================================================== account / privacy / terms
            $k('Do I have to agree to the activity recording?', 'agree recording, consent tracking, accept terms recording, privacy consent, activity tracking agree', 'Yes, it is part of the Terms and Privacy notice accepted when registering. It records pages, buttons and errors to give better help, never passwords or what you type into fields.'),
            $k('Who can see my activity history?', 'who sees my activity, activity visible, history visible admin, who can see what i do, privacy history', 'You can see your own history (History in the assistant). Administrators see summaries and, when you ask for help, what you did just before the problem.'),
